Hi,

Matt Molyneaux <moggers87-gM/Ye1E23mwN+BqQ9rBEUg@public.gmane.org> writes:

> Are there any Nouveau developers in Europe (preferably in the UK) who
> would like a GeForce 7600 GS? It's the AGP version and is no longer
> useful to me. I've got the power dongle (it requires a 350W power
> supply) and a S-Video to composite dongle.
>
> Specs:
> BFG GeForce 7600 GS OC (AGP)
> 512MB RAM
> DVI + VGA
> 1 x power dongle (the sort that plug into pata drives)
> 1 x "HDTV" dongle (S-Video to composite)

If component is what you meant (HDTV and composite in the same statement
is an oxymoron) I'm interested on it. I'm doing some work on TV out
support [1] and component output is mostly broken now because of lack of
hardware. If you actually meant composite, it might still support
component through a different adapter, some logs from X running with
nouveau would clear this up (you don't need the branch with TV out
support, master would do).

>
> It was working last time I tested it and has been in the box for ~ two
> years now. I am willing to post it, but only within Europe. If you're a
> developer outside of Europe I'm sure we can sort something out if no one
> else wants it.
>

I do live in Europe but not in the UK. I guess you should wait a week or
so because someone else might come up with a more interesting proposal.

